vocab.tsv
  Frequency ranks, parts of speech, transliterations and glosses for the 5,000
  most frequent Persian words. Glosses are the project's own wording.
  Homographs are split into separate lemmas; rare readings carry placeholder
  ranks at the end of the list until real frequencies are available.
  Since 18 Nov 2026 the ranks are the source list's ranks reweighted with
  spoken frequency (tools/fa_spoken_rerank): word counts from film and TV
  subtitles (OpenSubtitles 2018, via Hermit Dave's FrequencyWords) and from
  the wordfreq package (Robyn Speer; data CC BY-SA 4.0). The source ranks
  keep two thirds of the weight and are kept in
  tools/fa_spoken_rerank/miller_ranks.tsv. 98 everyday words missing from
  the source list were added with estimated ranks, tagged rank=estimated.
  No subtitle or wordfreq data is included here.
  Thirteen common words are not in the source frequency list: را, روی, کمی,
  شاید, نزد, لطفاً, بریدن, آفریدن, گریستن, باریدن, آویختن, برانگیختن,
  برافراشتن. Their ranks are estimates, tagged rank=estimated:
  each word's count in UD Persian-PerDT (all forms of the lemma), scaled to
  the source list's counts by the median ratio of 58 prepositions, adverbs and
  conjunctions found in both, then placed at the rank of the source words with
  the nearest counts. PerDT samples written Persian only (news, academic
  papers, magazine articles, fiction), so conversational words (لطفاً,
  شاید) are likely ranked too low.

grammar.yaml, config.yaml
  The project's own work. Levels follow the usual sequence of Persian-as-a-foreign-
  language courses and are provisional. Patterns were written against the output of
  Stanza's Persian model (trained on UD Persian-PerDT, CC BY-SA 4.0); no treebank
  data is included here. tools/fa_eval_perdt.py reads the treebank at run time.
